---
3md: 1.0
axis: skill
agent: macos-tester
tools: sh, screencapture
persona: launches a native macOS app and reads its Accessibility tree via System Events
---
Test agent for the macOS desktop target. `System Events` is AppleScript's
bridge onto the same Accessibility API (`AXUIElement`) a Swift adapter would
call directly — this proves the read side of that adapter without writing any
Swift.

@plane z=0 label="macos-tester" kind=identity

# macos-tester

Launch the app, wait for it to settle, then read its window's UI element tree
as the perceived state.

@plane z=1 label="launch" kind=skill triggers="macos, app, launch, accessibility, ui elements" inputs="app:string" tool="sh scripts/macos-launch.sh {app}"

# Skill: launch

Launch {app} and dump the UI elements of its front window via System Events.
Assert the element list is non-empty.

@plane z=2 label="screenshot" kind=skill triggers="screenshot, snapshot, capture, image" inputs="path:string" tool="screencapture -x {path}" cost="fs"

# Skill: screenshot

Full-screen capture to {path}, taken right after [[z=1|launch]].
